# Mediators example. Watch the console: every call prints a "Mediator.Send {Request}" span and,
# periodically, the viana.mediator.request.duration metric.
@host = http://localhost:5031

### List (200)
GET {{host}}/products

### Get (200) / missing (404)
GET {{host}}/products/1

###
GET {{host}}/products/99

### Create (201) – run twice to get a 409
POST {{host}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "HS-001", "name": "Headset", "price": 499.0, "stock": 5 }

### Create invalid (400 validation problem)
POST {{host}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "", "name": "", "price": 0, "stock": -1 }

### Update (204)
PUT {{host}}/products/2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "MS-002", "name": "Wireless mouse v2", "price": 139.9, "stock": 20 }

### Delete with stock (422) / without stock (204)
DELETE {{host}}/products/1

###
DELETE {{host}}/products/3

### ---------- Scenarios ----------

### Handler throws: 500 problem; span Error + exception event (see Mediator:Telemetry:ExceptionDetails)
GET {{host}}/scenarios/throws

### No handler registered: 500 problem naming the request and result types; span Error, error.type = HandlerNotFoundException
GET {{host}}/scenarios/unregistered

### Dependency down: 503 problem; span Error (5xx)
GET {{host}}/scenarios/unavailable

### Slow request: cancel it from the client before it ends; the span gets viana.mediator.cancelled and is not an error
GET {{host}}/scenarios/slow?seconds=10
